    "updated_at": "2026-11-20T20:20:33Z",
    "body": "Controller confirmed by the machine owner (MisterMaker on Discord, relayed by the user, 2026-11-20): an **Estlcam controller board running Estlcam's own control software**. This is Christian Knüll's German Estlcam, not grbl or the Ooznest BlackBox.\n\nWhat this means for the machine file:\n- The post is not grbl. Estlcam's PC software drives the board directly, and external G-code goes through Estlcam's own control program.\n- Still to confirm, from Estlcam's own documentation or a test file run by the owner:\n  - which G-code words its control program accepts from other CAM programs (arcs as G2/G3 with I/J or R, G90/G91, units, spindle words, comments, tool changes)\n  - its line-length and decimal limits\n  - whether it needs a specific file extension\n- Until then, the machine file should point at a conservative 3-axis post. Its programs should use only G0/G1/G2/G3 with I/J, G21 or G20, G90, M3/M5 and a feed, with no canned cycles or cutter compensation, so that the owner can test them.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
