    "updated_at": "2026-11-20T21:02:14Z",
    "body": "More from the owner (MisterMaker, relayed 2026-11-20):\n- **Frame and drive:** a WorkBee **1500 x 1000** (he thinks), driven by **TR8 trapezoidal lead screws**, not belts. TR8 screws limit rapids and feeds: set conservative maximum feeds in the machine file until he confirms them.\n- **Work area: 1200 x 800 mm** (X x Y). Z travel is still to confirm.\n- **Spindle: 2.2 kW**, most likely a VFD spindle; he calls it \"way overkill\". Still to confirm: the rpm range (typical 2.2 kW spindles run about 6,000-24,000 rpm, with poor torque at the low end), and whether Estlcam sets the rpm (S word) or the spindle is run by hand.\n- **Controller:** Estlcam board with Estlcam software. He doesn't know which G-code Estlcam accepts from other CAM programs. He notes the hardware is open source. The accepted words still have to come from Estlcam's documentation or a test file he runs.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
