    "updated_at": "2026-11-20T21:02:51Z",
    "body": "Estlcam's hardware page (https://www.estlcam.de/hardware.php, read 2026-11-20; German) says:\n- **Boards:** Estlcam's own controller boards are open-source hardware: a KiCAD 8 project, free for personal and commercial use.\n- **Variants:** \"Terminal Adapter\" (XL, M, Light) and LPT/parallel-port adapters, built on an **AVR64DB64** microcontroller.\n- **Firmware:** the page welcomes ports of GRBL to the boards, as long as the bootloader is kept, but it gives no firmware licence.\n- **Not covered:** none of the pages read (hardware, index, estlcam, changelog) says which G-code from other CAM programs Estlcam runs, which words it accepts, or how the spindle is controlled. Those still need Estlcam's manual or help pages, or a test file run by the owner.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
